This study introduces a groundbreaking singing voice conversion (SVC) approach that leverages denoising diffusion probabilistic models (DPMs) to generate high-quality converted voices. Building on the success of diffusion models in producing realistic results, our method incorporates a singing-specific enhancement module to further improve performance. To facilitate the development of singing models, we introduce a novel dataset of 40-speaker demos, each paired with a professional singer. Experimental outcomes confirm the effectiveness of our DPM-based SVC approach, yielding superior voice quality and outperforming existing methods in terms of conversion accuracy and singing-related metrics. Moreover, our method's adaptability is showcased through its ability to successfully convert popular singer voices. Notably, our approach sets a new benchmark in the field, achieving state-of-the-art performance on the VoiceCloning Challenge 2021 leaderboard. The project's code and datasets are publicly available on GitHub. \href{https://github.com/ChenFulong/DiffSVC}{https://github.com/ChenFulong/DiffSVC}. A demo can be accessed at \href{https://sfcvst.surge.sh/}{https://sfcvst.surge.sh/}. \end{document} 
